CORE
main.bash
--show-parse-tree
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^    word lit"export"$
^    word lit"A=1"$
^    word lit"B"$
^    word dq\(param\(C\)\)$
^    word lit"D=" param\(x\)$
^    word lit"E="$
^    word lit"readonly"$
^    word lit"R=~/x"$
^    word lit"local"$
^    word lit"l=" param\(1\)$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
In the bash dialect shfmt parses declaration utilities as DeclClause; the
reader rebuilds the simple command that the POSIX dialect yields (see
declaration-utilities-posix), so that later stages apply XCU 2.9.1.1 by
command name.
